<item><title>Request for Information - Cyber Security Dashboard</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Queensland Government is seeking information from the market to better understand available products, services and delivery approaches that could support an executive-level cyber security dashboard and/or reporting capability.<br /><br />The intended capability would provide executive government with a consolidated view of the cyber security position across Queensland Government budget sector agencies, with potential future expansion to include Government Owned Corporations (GOCs) and statutory authorities. The current budget sector comprises approximately 21 agencies/entities, with a broader future scope potentially including statutory authorities, in addition to relevant GOCs.<br /><br />Queensland Government agencies operate in a complex and diverse digital environment, with varying business functions, risk profiles, technology landscapes and levels of cyber security maturity. Cyber security information is often generated through a range of sources, including assessments, assurance activities, operatio...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Customer, Data and Small Business (CDSB)<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 30/Oct/2026 03:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP525921<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : IT & Telecomms<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 1]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.com.au/tsi.axd?id=89fc14384cfb4f65aeb4cb7308f01978s525921se5e0fee99bee4eef813ebcd8f1872d76s1578</link>
