<item><title>New Reservoir at Bamaga</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Northern Peninsular Area Council is looking to expand the amount of storage available at their Bamaga Reservoir site.<br /><br />At present there are 2 x 1.6ML concrete tanks that receive water via the Clear Water Pump Station at our Water Treatment Plant.<br /><br />We would like to increase supply by at least another 1.6ML in size.<br /><br />The top water level would need to be the same as the existing reservoirs.<br /><br />This will be a design/ construct project, with the design needing to be approved by Council before proceeding to the construction phase.<br /><br />We are expecting the design and planning work to happen during the upcoming wet season, with construction starting in May/ June 2027. <br /><br />Level Sensors and Outlet Flow Meter will be provided as part of this contract. Council will ensure these are integrated into our SCADA system.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Northern Peninsula Area Regional Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 18/Oct/2026 05:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP525865<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Steve Martin Email: steve.martin@nparc.qld.gov.au Tel: 0486 318 882<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Water & Sewage<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 2]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.com.au/tsi.axd?id=08b06828435a4bf88f31fcc25290c622s525865s786e232eacbb4e31b23c50bf234a0226s1611</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">08b06828435a4bf88f31fcc25290c622</guid>
<pubDate>Wed, 16 Sep 2026 04:44:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>Water &amp; Sewage</category>
</item>
<item><title>EXC00132 Request for Quote Digital Asset Management Solution</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Council invites suitably qualified suppliers to propose a secure, scalable Digital Asset Management solution to manage the full digital content lifecycle. The successful supplier <br /><br />will design, configure, integrate and migrate existing assets. Responses must show how the solution meets Council’s operational, technical, governance, cyber security, data, records, authentication and accessibility requirements. <br /><br />Suppliers must outline their implementation approach, support model, service levels, governance arrangements and all related costs. Responses must also explain how the <br /><br />solution will support administration, upgrades, user adoption, growing asset volumes, automated tagging, artificial intelligence assisted search and multi channel distribution.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Townsville City Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 08/Oct/2026 12:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP525872<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : IT & Telecomms<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 3]]></description>
