<item><title>Bruce Highway Targeted Safety Program Independent Financial Auditor Panel</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Department of Transport and Main Roads (TMR) is delivering the Bruce Highway Targeted Safety Program (BHTSP). The Bruce Highway is a vital 1,673 kilometre north-south corridor in Queensland, connecting Brisbane to Cairns. In January 2025, the Australian and Queensland governments announced a joint funding commitment of $9 billion towards the BHTSP to enhance safety and uplift deficient sections of the highway to achieve a three-star rating.<br /><br />The BHTSP focuses on sections of the Bruce Highway between Gympie and Cairns with a high safety risk.<br /><br />Financial audits to be delivered through the BHTSP will be awarded to prequalified members on the Independent Financial Auditor (IFA) Panel. The BHTSP will be delivered in the following districts:<br /><br />- Far North Queensland District<br /><br />- Fitzroy District<br /><br />- Mackay/Whitsunday District<br /><br />- Northern District<br /><br />- Wide Bay/Burnett District<br /><br />IFA Panel Member may be engaged to deliver a project under a...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Department of Transport and Main Roads<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 25/Sep/2026 11:00 AM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP525563<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Stephen How Lum Email: steve.f.howlum@tmr.qld.gov.au Tel: 0468330611<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 6]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.com.au/tsi.axd?id=1ff69532502940508f32dccd0f0da777s525563s50c818bb80c044cab1c37a23ba39eee8s1554</link>
