<item><title>DLGWV2026-0351 Design and Construction of the Mapoon New Treated Water Reservoir Project</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Department of Local Government, Water and Volunteers (DLGWV) is seeking to engage a suitably qualified and experienced contractor to undertake the Design and Construction of the Mapoon New Treated Water Reservoir Project. The works includes geotechnical investigations and surveying to support the design of a new treated water reservoir and future upgrades to the Water Treatment Plant (WTP). The scope of works also includes the demolition and removal of the existing steel structure, relocation of two sheds for repurposing by Council, remediation of the existing 1.2 ML concrete reservoir, and the design, supply, delivery, construction, installation, testing, commissioning, and performance testing of a new treated water reservoir.<br /><br />Tenderers are to refer to Invitation to Offer documents for further details. <br /><br />A non-mandatory Industry Briefing will be held at 10:30am AEST, 16 September 2026. Tenderers are required to register their attendance by sending an email to Procurement@dlgwv.qld.go...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Dept of Local Government Water and Volunteers<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 07/Oct/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP523022<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation, Engineer, Research, Tech services, Utilities, Water & Sewage<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 13]]></description>
