<item><title>TEN16730 - Mount Morgan Cemetery Extension</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Mount Morgan Cemetery is a heritage listed cemetery located at East Street, Mount Morgan, within the Rockhampton Region, Queensland. Established in 1886, the cemetery has served the Mount Morgan community for the majority of the town’s history and was entered on the Queensland Heritage Register on 21 October 1992. The site contains numerous memorials, structures, and landscape elements of historical, cultural, social, and aesthetic significance, including the Linda Memorial and a rare Chinese ceremonial burner.<br /><br />The land formerly identified as Lot 3614 has undergone a boundary realignment along East Street South and has been consolidated with Lot 184 to form a single allotment. More recently, the consolidated site has been rezoned to Community to support and facilitate the proposed extension of the Mount Morgan Cemetery. This technical specification has been prepared to support the delivery of civil works associated with the cemetery extension, which is intended to provide additional burial capacity...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Rockhampton Regional Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 30/Sep/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP524573<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 1]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.com.au/tsi.axd?id=c58b3852d32a4f1ba574200c7c24632as524573s50c818bb80c044cab1c37a23ba39eee8s1554</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">c58b3852d32a4f1ba574200c7c24632a</guid>
<pubDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 23:05:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>Construction &amp; Operation</category>
</item>
<item><title>Principal Contractor for Stage 2 - Balcony Repairs at Hill Houses - Thursday Is</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> •	Remove and dispose of the existing balcony handrails and non-compliant horizontal balustrade systems <br /><br />•	Supply and install new compliant hot dip galvanised balustrade and handrail systems incorporating vertical balusters to all nominated balconies in accordance with the National Construction Code (NCC) and relevant Australian Standards. <br /><br />•	Inspect existing balcony structures, including joists, bearers, decking, steelwork, fixings and supporting members, for deterioration or structural defects prior to installation of the new balustrade system.<br /><br />•	Replace or rectify any deteriorated or defective structural members identified during construction where required to facilitate a compliant installation. Any major structural defects identified beyond the scope shall be reported to the Principal for direction prior to proceeding.<br /><br />•	Modify existing privacy screen framing where required to remove climbable elements and install compliant vertical screening while retaining the...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Torres and Cape Hospital and Health Service<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 22/Sep/2026 11:00 AM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP523813<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Building Trade, Repairs, Maint., Construction & Operation<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 1]]></description>
