<item><title>Rubber Softfall Renewal - Emerald Botanical Gardens and Rotary Park Blackwater</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Council requires the supply and installation of certified impact-attenuating rubber softfall surfacing in the form of a modular individual tile system at existing playgrounds including approximately 300m2 at the Emerald Regional Botanic Gardens and approximately 400m2 at Rotary Park, Blackwater. <br /><br />The installed softfall system must be certified to comply with the relevant Australian Standards for impact attenuation and playground safety, including the required Critical Fall Height for the playground equipment. The finished motif is to be a like for like pattern using the existing colour palette. The surface is to be uniform, free from trip hazards and constructed to the required levels and drainage requirements.<br /><br />The contractor is to provide all labour, plant, equipment, materials, testing, certification and associated works necessary to deliver a fully compliant and completed installation. Temporary construction fencing to fully isolate the project area from public access is to be supplie...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Central Highlands Regional Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 28/Sep/2026 12:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP523808<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Sport, Recreation Equip, Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 4]]></description>
<link>https://www.vendorpanel.com.au/tsi.axd?id=5f1c1ad2c46e4450a4039fb8a1af076cs523808sbfe2d966aa884191b5a30f84da5d0f3fs1604</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">5f1c1ad2c46e4450a4039fb8a1af076c</guid>
<pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2026 19:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
<category>Sport, Recreation Equip, Services</category>
</item>
<item><title>Central Queensland Hospital and Health Service (CQHHS) Condition Assessment Audit 2026-2029</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The State of Queensland through Queensland Health (the Client), invites you to submit an offer for the provision of suitably qualified and experienced consultant to undertake comprehensive condition assessments of Queensland Health assets for the Central Queensland Hospital and Health Service CQHHS Condition Assessment Audit 2026-2029 Project in accordance with the Invitation documents.<br /><br />The purpose of this Scope of Works is to engage suitably qualified and experienced consultants to undertake comprehensive condition assessments of Queensland Health assets. The assessments will provide accurate, consistent and auditable information on asset condition, remaining useful life, defects, risks and renewal requirements. This information will support strategic asset management, maintenance planning, capital investment planning and long-term infrastructure renewal across Queensland Health.<br /><br />For detailed information on the specific goods / services sought under this Request for Offer, please review...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Health Infrastructure Queensland<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 22/Sep/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP524007<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Justin Acutt Email: justin.acutt@health.qld.gov.au Tel: 0487438411<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Architecture, Design, Planning, Construction & Operation, Engineer, Research, Tech services, Real Estate & Property Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 15]]></description>
