<item><title>Tropical Cyclone Alfred Environmental Recovery Program, Catchment Rehabilitation Program</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> The Department of the Environment, Tourism, Science and Innovation invites Offers from eligible Suppliers for the provision of services to support catchment rehabilitation following the Tropical Cyclone Alfred and Associated Severe Weather, March 1 – 16 2025.<br /><br />The objective of this Invitation to Offer (ITO) process is to engage eligible Suppliers across the 18 impacted Local Government Areas (LGA’s) to support the delivery of catchment rehabilitation projects that deliver on-ground catchment rehabilitation efforts that meet the objectives and outcomes, eligibility criteria and timeframes of the DRFA funding allocation. Proposed projects must support disaster recovery activities as a result of impacts caused by Tropical Cyclone Alfred and Associated Severe Weather, March 1 – 16 2025.<br /><br />Eligibility - Please note that Suppliers and projects offered through this ITO process are required to meet eligibility requirements outlined within Part A - Invitation to Offer, Attachment C - Eligibility Det...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Dept of the Environ, Tourism, Science and Innov<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 08/Oct/2026 02:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP523874<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Environmental & Heritage Services<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 10]]></description>
