<item><title>Ports North Tingira Street – 2026 Surcharge Relocation and Gravel Pavement Works</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Far North Queensland Ports Corporation Limited, trading as Ports North (PN) is a government-owned Corporation established under the Government Owned Corporations Act 1993 (Qld) that develops and manages Port facilities. PN operates the Ports of Cairns, Cape Flattery, Karumba, Mourilyan, Skardon River, Quintell Beach, Thursday Island, Burketown and Cooktown. <br /><br /> <br /><br />Ports North invites Tenders from Civil Construction Contractors for a project in the Port of Cairns. The project’s scope of work includes the relocation two separate surcharge stockpiles and the repair and augmentation of pavement gravel to an existing storage yard.<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Far North Queensland Ports Corporation Ltd<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 23/Sep/2026 04:00 PM (UTC+10:00) Brisbane time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP523896<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 14]]></description>
