<item><title>Demolition of the Botany Administration Building - 141 Coward St, Mascot, NSW</title>
<description><![CDATA[<b>Tender Details : </b> Bayside Council invites suitably qualified and experienced contractors to submit a quotation for the demolition of the former Botany Administration Building located at 141 Coward Street, Mascot. The project involves the demolition and removal of the existing three-storey building, associated awnings, water tank and ground floor slab, together with site remediation, clearing and regrading works. The scope also includes the design, supply and installation of new perimeter palisade fencing and gates, and the placement of a crushed aggregate capping layer.<br /><br />The site is generally level and is located between two locally listed heritage items, Coronation Hall and the Mascot Fire Station, requiring careful management of demolition activities and environmental controls. Existing footings and foundations are to remain in situ, and no works are required within the existing hardstand car parking area.<br /><br />A mandatory site inspection will be held on site Monday 31 August 2026, at 11.00am. Please note tha...<br /><br /><b>Issued by : </b> Bayside Council<br /><b>Closing Date</b> : 22/Sep/2026 10:00 AM (UTC+10:00) Canberra, Melbourne, Sydney time<br /><b>Reference number</b> : VP522363<br /><b>Contact person</b> : Not disclosed<br /><b>Tender categories</b> : Construction & Operation<br /><b>Specification Docs</b> : 11]]></description>
